reated as functionally identical the outputs might be logically linked instead.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm checking whether the twin's action counts as a child of my fdt node, since the two copies only differ in names and lead text. I'm working through the essay's recipe of making a node for each input the processes evaluate, so that my action comes out as fdt(x) while the other copy evaluates fdt on its own input.\n\nI'm weighing whether the twin's action should be treated as a child of my fdt node, or as a separate node fdt(y) that A-FDT holds fixed. Holding the other copy's output fixed, defecting dominates, so the coordinate-wise reading gives mutual defection, though if the two inputs were treated as functionally identical the outputs might be logically linked instead.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10183,"completion_tokens":854,"total_tokens":11037,"cost":0.057812,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.057812,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.040732,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01708},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":504,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}